 is 108\u00b0F, on July 13, 1980.","t_chg":"Macon's nights cooled over the long run. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 126 complete years: Macon's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.17 to \u22120.05), about \u22121.4\u00b0F since 1900. Macon's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.24 to +0.35), about +3.7\u00b0F since 1900.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 6 months fell. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Macon's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.26 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 46.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 2013 (72.67 in); the driest, 1954 (26.05 in). Macon almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.4 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}